{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Disgrace.</b> For all generations; this is the meaning of \"for he committed an outrage in Israel,\"" "And the meaning of \"va-yedabberu asher timei\" — \"va-yedabberu et Shekhem asher timei their sister,\" for we find \"dibberu le-shalom\" (Genesis 37:4) like \"dibber lo,\" or the meaning of \"asher\" is that they answered with guile because he defiled:" "<b>Who has an foreskin.</b> A foreskin of flesh, and its meaning is something that is heavy/blocking; likewise \"aral sefatayim\" (Exodus 6:12), \"arlah oznam\" (Jeremiah 6:10), because of the addition. And those who say that HaShem said to Abraham \"and be whole\" (Genesis 17:1), and when he is circumcised he is lacking — the matter is the opposite, and behold the animals will prove it. And if they say, why should something that HaShem created be cut off, even the navel will prove it."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:01.641656814Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}